(2047833, 281184, 24913, '<td valign="top">Beautiful lighting and lashes!</td>', 'Beautiful lighting and lashes!', '2006-01-17 11:29:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(2047834, 275350, 19831, '<td valign="top">Very interesting subject. Might make for a stronger photo if you got in tight, and made the shot more about the sand balls. Attention is drawn away by all the swimmers and the water. The blue object on the left edge of frame seems to be a bit distracting. The sky is nice and dramatic, with great color. The island thingies in the distance are nice and interesting, neat how the sand pile is centered between them. The point of view here is kind of mundane though, seen from where anyone could just stand and look at the scene, often times when a photo shows an un-ordinary angle or view, something one wouldn''t normally see, it can add a lot of interest to a photo. I''m thinking maybe if this were a vertical ''portrait'' crop, shot from a lower point of view, keeping the tower centered and leading towards the islands, and still showing that great sky, it could be a much stronger presentation. I know that doesn''t help much with this shot, (although you could still try a vertical crop if it sounds like an idea with potential to you), but maybe something to keep in mind in the future :-)</td>', 'Very interesting subject. Might make for a stronger photo if you got in tight, and made the shot more about the sand balls. Attention is drawn away by all the swimmers and the water. The blue object on the left edge of frame seems to be a bit distracting. The sky is nice and dramatic, with great color. The island thingies in the distance are nice and interesting, neat how the sand pile is centered between them. The point of view here is kind of mundane though, seen from where anyone could just stand and look at the scene, often times when a photo shows an un-ordinary angle or view, something one wouldn''t normally see, it can add a lot of interest to a photo. I''m thinking maybe if this were a vertical ''portrait'' crop, shot from a lower point of view, keeping the tower centered and leading towards the islands, and still showing that great sky, it could be a much stronger presentation. I know that doesn''t help much with this shot, (although you could still try a vertical crop if it sounds like an idea with potential to you), but maybe something to keep in mind in the future :-)', '2006-01-17 11:29:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(2047838, 274790, 34413, '<td valign="top">Awesome shot!</td>', 'Awesome shot!', '2006-01-17 11:30:21.000000', NULL, 1),
