(2063169, 281529, 42792, '<td valign="top">The 2 basic things that instantly marr this photo is the light and how it''s composed.  It''s so dark that all details of the bird are lost and yet it can''t pass off as an interesting and clean silhouette.  Composition is usually (altho'' not in all cases) more interesting if you follow the Rule of Thirds.  Here you could probably position the bird more to the left on an imaginary vertical third of the frame because it''s facing right.  Let me know if you''d like some help. I''m no expert but a couple of basic things can certainly be done here to show you instantly a difference.</td>', 'The 2 basic things that instantly marr this photo is the light and how it''s composed.  It''s so dark that all details of the bird are lost and yet it can''t pass off as an interesting and clean silhouette.  Composition is usually (altho'' not in all cases) more interesting if you follow the Rule of Thirds.  Here you could probably position the bird more to the left on an imaginary vertical third of the frame because it''s facing right.  Let me know if you''d like some help. I''m no expert but a couple of basic things can certainly be done here to show you instantly a difference.', '2006-01-20 09:11:10.000000', NULL, 1),
