(2069031, 279380, 17507, '<td valign="top">here''s a slightly pedantic but grammatically correct point of potential interest to some.<br/> <br/>I take it that the title is meant to indicate the baby''s reaction to her grandmother. In order for this to be expressed correctly, the title should be "That tickles, Grandma," because "Grandma" functions as a vocative (the person being addressed) and not as the object of the verb "tickles."<br/> <br/>As it stands, the title says that "That" (presumably the baby) is currently tickling Grandma. I can imagine someone picking the baby up and rubbing it against Grandma, because the baby tickles grandma and makes her giggle. In this respect, the baby is kind of like a long piece of grass.<br/> <br/>I suppose that''s not what you meant, though</td>', 'here''s a slightly pedantic but grammatically correct point of potential interest to some. I take it that the title is meant to indicate the baby''s reaction to her grandmother. In order for this to be expressed correctly, the title should be "That tickles, Grandma," because "Grandma" functions as a vocative (the person being addressed) and not as the object of the verb "tickles." As it stands, the title says that "That" (presumably the baby) is currently tickling Grandma. I can imagine someone picking the baby up and rubbing it against Grandma, because the baby tickles grandma and makes her giggle. In this respect, the baby is kind of like a long piece of grass. I suppose that''s not what you meant, though', '2006-01-21 21:12:18.000000', NULL, 1),
