(2086886, 276752, 38032, '<td valign="top">I''m tring to put a finger on why this is so ikeable ... I think the extreme contrast from sun to shadow and then to the extreme dark shadow on the left and in the distance creates drama.  The over-hill horizon feeling adds to the emotion like heading up a roller coaster.  You did well not to oversharpen this since it is more about light than the details of the objects.  Very nice.  9</td>', 'I''m tring to put a finger on why this is so ikeable ... I think the extreme contrast from sun to shadow and then to the extreme dark shadow on the left and in the distance creates drama.  The over-hill horizon feeling adds to the emotion like heading up a roller coaster.  You did well not to oversharpen this since it is more about light than the details of the objects.  Very nice.  9', '2006-01-26 07:35:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(2086887, 280921, 19831, '<td valign="top">I have saved this photo to the last of my voting. I have viewed it several times since the voting stage began. I find it to be one of the most interesting images in this challenge in an odd, quirky, intriguing kind of way. It is either pure genius or pure rubbish, or somewhere in between :-) Technically wise, it does seem like the focus could be just a tad sharper, perhaps a little usm would help. The color does look quite good. Lighting is even, but certainly not dramatic, but I don''t think it needs to be for this image. I see no harsh shadows or hot spots. I am thinking that compositionally, perhaps it could be strengthened by cropping out the mop bucket, or maybe better yet to include all of it. Maybe not? I do give kudos for producing (at least to me) a refreshing and unique, thought provoking photo, although it may be something that does not appeal to the masses. Good luck in the challenge :-)</td>', 'I have saved this photo to the last of my voting. I have viewed it several times since the voting stage began. I find it to be one of the most interesting images in this challenge in an odd, quirky, intriguing kind of way. It is either pure genius or pure rubbish, or somewhere in between :-) Technically wise, it does seem like the focus could be just a tad sharper, perhaps a little usm would help. The color does look quite good. Lighting is even, but certainly not dramatic, but I don''t think it needs to be for this image. I see no harsh shadows or hot spots. I am thinking that compositionally, perhaps it could be strengthened by cropping out the mop bucket, or maybe better yet to include all of it. Maybe not? I do give kudos for producing (at least to me) a refreshing and unique, thought provoking photo, although it may be something that does not appeal to the masses. Good luck in the challenge :-)', '2006-01-26 07:35:59.000000', NULL, 1),
