(2108571, 280366, 12160, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by dudephil:</b></div><hr/><i> This is very cool! I''d love to see the original. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for your comments. Here''s the original shot resized for web.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=289484" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/12160/thumb/289484.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/12160/thumb/289484.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/12160/thumb/289484.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Originally posted by dudephil: This is very cool! I''d love to see the original.   Thanks for your comments. Here''s the original shot resized for web.', '2006-02-01 03:16:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2108590, 274637, 47377, '<td valign="top">thanks for the comments.<br/>a couple od people commented on using the full 640px limit... I have!<br/>and the grain... well that''s just the way the fabrix was that I used.<br/>I didn''t feel like it was a problem, but I just might try and remove some of it to see if I like the picture any better!<br/>Ingrid.</td>', 'thanks for the comments.a couple od people commented on using the full 640px limit... I have!and the grain... well that''s just the way the fabrix was that I used.I didn''t feel like it was a problem, but I just might try and remove some of it to see if I like the picture any better!Ingrid.', '2006-02-01 03:21:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2108599, 281042, 37252, '<td valign="top">Nice finish JP! Beautiful image you can always be proud of. Congrats on 36th place out of 829 entries!! What a wonderful compliment to your work.</td>', 'Nice finish JP! Beautiful image you can always be proud of. Congrats on 36th place out of 829 entries!! What a wonderful compliment to your work.', '2006-02-01 03:23:39.000000', NULL, 0),
