(2109670, 281383, 42013, '<td valign="top">I suspected this would get hit with some anti-American sentiment.  I guess we all vote with hearts on some level.  Great job and deserved a higher placing. I''d like to think if I saw a well-done picture of another country''s flag I would vote "somewhat" objectively.  Otherwise, this is less about photography and more about a personal political statement.</td>', 'I suspected this would get hit with some anti-American sentiment.  I guess we all vote with hearts on some level.  Great job and deserved a higher placing. I''d like to think if I saw a well-done picture of another country''s flag I would vote "somewhat" objectively.  Otherwise, this is less about photography and more about a personal political statement.', '2006-02-01 09:34:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2109744, 276106, 47169, '<td valign="top">hugely under-rated in my opinion. i really love this photo. the tones and dof are perfect. well done indeed</td>', 'hugely under-rated in my opinion. i really love this photo. the tones and dof are perfect. well done indeed', '2006-02-01 09:50:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2109753, 277650, 14476, '<td valign="top">I''m going to disagree with the crowd on this one.  The soft focus works well for me in this portrait.  It would go well with the Modern Art crowd and I hope you enjoy this fine image for what it is.<br/> <br/>Keep the unusual ones coming!</td>', 'I''m going to disagree with the crowd on this one.  The soft focus works well for me in this portrait.  It would go well with the Modern Art crowd and I hope you enjoy this fine image for what it is. Keep the unusual ones coming!', '2006-02-01 09:53:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(2109780, 280577, 29556, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by livitup:</b></div><hr/><i> I wish this had been a stop-action (perhaps with the feet blurred) rather than using post processing to add &lt;&lt;more&gt;&gt; blur (at least that''s what I assume happened here. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Actually, nothing was added to this photo. For me, that is what made it special. I did brighten it up a little but other than that...this is the original.</td>', 'Originally posted by livitup: I wish this had been a stop-action (perhaps with the feet blurred) rather than using post processing to add <<more>> blur (at least that''s what I assume happened here.   Actually, nothing was added to this photo. For me, that is what made it special. I did brighten it up a little but other than that...this is the original.', '2006-02-01 10:00:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2109790, 281437, 13879, '<td valign="top">I really like this shot, I hoped it would have done better. Keep up the good work!</td>', 'I really like this shot, I hoped it would have done better. Keep up the good work!', '2006-02-01 10:03:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2109791, 280577, 29556, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by confused:</b></div><hr/><i> Did you go to the zoo to get this picture </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I expected to finish better considering I lost an arm trying to get this shot... Just kidding. :) Yes, I shot this from about 150ft at the zoo.</td>', 'Originally posted by confused: Did you go to the zoo to get this picture   I expected to finish better considering I lost an arm trying to get this shot... Just kidding. :) Yes, I shot this from about 150ft at the zoo.', '2006-02-01 10:03:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2109795, 279850, 31443, '<td valign="top">Should have known this was yours Lynnesite! What a magnificent beast!</td>', 'Should have known this was yours Lynnesite! What a magnificent beast!', '2006-02-01 10:04:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2109798, 280577, 29556, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by DanSig:</b></div><hr/><i> this is without a doubt the worst lion picture in this challenge, you can show movement without having the subject moved, try paning, that way you get the lion frozen in focus but the surrounding moved to show speed. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>and<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by fotodude:</b></div><hr/><i> i love the motion, this truly counts a a top noutch art shot. maybe 1 of the best motion shots on this entire site. looks like a Michael Nichols (last place on earth) shot...really great Good Luck </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Seems like people loved it or hated it. :) Thanks for all of the comments. These helped a lot.</td>', 'Originally posted by DanSig: this is without a doubt the worst lion picture in this challenge, you can show movement without having the subject moved, try paning, that way you get the lion frozen in focus but the surrounding moved to show speed.   and Originally posted by fotodude: i love the motion, this truly counts a a top noutch art shot. maybe 1 of the best motion shots on this entire site. looks like a Michael Nichols (last place on earth) shot...really great Good Luck   Seems like people loved it or hated it. :) Thanks for all of the comments. These helped a lot.', '2006-02-01 10:05:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(2109822, 278837, 45754, '<td valign="top">I just want to thank everyone for all the nice comments and votes on my photo. This won the Merit award in the B&amp;W Magazine''s Single Image Contest Annual 2005. It was chosen as one of 200 images to be published out of over 5,000 images entered and 900 photographers. I was very honored even to get the Merit. And I am honored you all liked it enough to vote on it. The original colored version is in my portfolio if anyone would like to see it.  Thanks again, it was fun.</td>', 'I just want to thank everyone for all the nice comments and votes on my photo. This won the Merit award in the B&W Magazine''s Single Image Contest Annual 2005. It was chosen as one of 200 images to be published out of over 5,000 images entered and 900 photographers. I was very honored even to get the Merit. And I am honored you all liked it enough to vote on it. The original colored version is in my portfolio if anyone would like to see it.  Thanks again, it was fun.', '2006-02-01 10:10:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(2109885, 277676, 19178, '<td valign="top">Neil, Congratulations on this wonderful finish and great shot!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-02-01 18:23:54.</i></td>', 'Neil, Congratulations on this wonderful finish and great shot!', '2006-02-01 10:19:18.000000', '2006-02-01 18:23:54.000000', 0),
(2109914, 281268, 48248, '<td valign="top">I''m no expert on post-editing techniques, so I''m not going to attempt to tell you how to do it... but, I feel like this image needs less sharpening in the forground (the granularity of the snow/ice is almost distracting), and the lighthouse needs to be brought out more (maybe more DOF and use of curves).  Nice composition</td>', 'I''m no expert on post-editing techniques, so I''m not going to attempt to tell you how to do it... but, I feel like this image needs less sharpening in the forground (the granularity of the snow/ice is almost distracting), and the lighthouse needs to be brought out more (maybe more DOF and use of curves).  Nice composition', '2006-02-01 10:23:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(2109938, 281484, 48248, '<td valign="top">I think this should have ranked much higher than 166th.  I can''t find anything wrong with this image.  The lighting and use of space is spectacular.  Maybe the subject wasn''t interesting enough for the voters.  I gave it a 10.</td>', 'I think this should have ranked much higher than 166th.  I can''t find anything wrong with this image.  The lighting and use of space is spectacular.  Maybe the subject wasn''t interesting enough for the voters.  I gave it a 10.', '2006-02-01 10:27:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2109976, 281845, 48248, '<td valign="top">This is one of a few in this challenge that I can''t figure out why it didn''t place much higher.  The DOF is perfect and the color balance is just enough to give it life without overdoing it (something I feel like is too often done with floral shots).</td>', 'This is one of a few in this challenge that I can''t figure out why it didn''t place much higher.  The DOF is perfect and the color balance is just enough to give it life without overdoing it (something I feel like is too often done with floral shots).', '2006-02-01 10:33:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(2109997, 279372, 48248, '<td valign="top">Great subject and title.  A bit out of focus, though.</td>', 'Great subject and title.  A bit out of focus, though.', '2006-02-01 10:36:30.000000', NULL, 0),
