(2111011, 274554, 41337, '<td valign="top">Gave this a 9. Surprised it ranked 101st.</td>', 'Gave this a 9. Surprised it ranked 101st.', '2006-02-01 14:45:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2111025, 276779, 7743, '<td valign="top">*** Self Critique ***<br/> <br/>Colours are vibrant and there is a sense of openness yet the bees are going about their activity with out notice of the background.<br/> <br/>That being the message I was trying to portray I think the flower and the bees need to be sharper.<br/> <br/>The bench is a major element yet detracts the viewer from the main intended content as does the flower in the lower right.  The flower could be cropped without losing anything.<br/> <br/>As far as making the bench less distracting, possibly trying for a slightly different angle to include less of it and more of the trees in the background.  Also, more dof would give more definition to the background and possibly make it less distracting.<br/> <br/>All in all, something to try again come spring.</td>', '*** Self Critique *** Colours are vibrant and there is a sense of openness yet the bees are going about their activity with out notice of the background. That being the message I was trying to portray I think the flower and the bees need to be sharper. The bench is a major element yet detracts the viewer from the main intended content as does the flower in the lower right.  The flower could be cropped without losing anything. As far as making the bench less distracting, possibly trying for a slightly different angle to include less of it and more of the trees in the background.  Also, more dof would give more definition to the background and possibly make it less distracting. All in all, something to try again come spring.', '2006-02-01 14:50:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(2111079, 277475, 40718, '<td valign="top">I like your choice of log as a subject.  It looks nice and weathered and contrasty.  A few things that make this shot a challenge:<br/> <br/>1) It doesn''t wow us with either texture or color.  The blue of the sky is, to me, my least favorite shade.  Evergreens, I have found, are almost impossible to make look good on a picture.  I haven''t figured that problem out yet myself.  Actually, your pine is pretty nice, but the bushes in the background suffer a similar problem, they quickly turn into a greenish/black mush which isn''t too fun to look at.  The texture is nice in a way, but also the grass gets lost in a mishmash of lines.  I bet the grass would actually look fairly nice on a canvas much bigger than 640 px.<br/> <br/>2) You have one half of a nice landscape; and it''s usually the half people forget, a foreground subject.  However, the background (once you remove the log) is fairly nondescript.  For the picture to soar we need to grow a mountain or something back there (which of course you can''t do).  perhaps more sky and some interesting clouds on a different day.<br/> <br/>People were pretty tough voting.  They wanted a WOW picture and I''m afraid this couldn''t deliver those goods.<br/></td>', 'I like your choice of log as a subject.  It looks nice and weathered and contrasty.  A few things that make this shot a challenge: 1) It doesn''t wow us with either texture or color.  The blue of the sky is, to me, my least favorite shade.  Evergreens, I have found, are almost impossible to make look good on a picture.  I haven''t figured that problem out yet myself.  Actually, your pine is pretty nice, but the bushes in the background suffer a similar problem, they quickly turn into a greenish/black mush which isn''t too fun to look at.  The texture is nice in a way, but also the grass gets lost in a mishmash of lines.  I bet the grass would actually look fairly nice on a canvas much bigger than 640 px. 2) You have one half of a nice landscape; and it''s usually the half people forget, a foreground subject.  However, the background (once you remove the log) is fairly nondescript.  For the picture to soar we need to grow a mountain or something back there (which of course you can''t do).  perhaps more sky and some interesting clouds on a different day. People were pretty tough voting.  They wanted a WOW picture and I''m afraid this couldn''t deliver those goods.', '2006-02-01 15:03:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2111131, 279719, 13384, '<td valign="top">Obviously a scanned image, and not a decent one at that.</td>', 'Obviously a scanned image, and not a decent one at that.', '2006-02-01 15:19:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(2111144, 281120, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by train:</b></div><hr/><i> This looks stunning why didnt you crop it in to gets rid of the distactions of the back ground  Its quite hard to focus on the actual image of the flower and butterfly<br/>Detail is great just that background is not </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I have been trying to concentrate on my camera skills and not editing, so I''ve been submitting a lot of uncropped shots just to see how successful my composition has been. I was actually very happy to achieve the DOF/bokeh effect, as it''s hard to do with this camera. I like the riotous colors, though they do provide camouflage, they also mimic/mirror the colors of the subject.<br/> <br/>Another consideration is that this is only a 3MP original -- cropping would probably limit me to 5x7 prints, even with a border.<br/> <br/>I can try fading the BG to make the butterfly pop out a bit more, and maybe I''ll try a vertical crop as well -- thanks for the sugggestion.</td>', 'Originally posted by train: This looks stunning why didnt you crop it in to gets rid of the distactions of the back ground  Its quite hard to focus on the actual image of the flower and butterflyDetail is great just that background is not  I have been trying to concentrate on my camera skills and not editing, so I''ve been submitting a lot of uncropped shots just to see how successful my composition has been. I was actually very happy to achieve the DOF/bokeh effect, as it''s hard to do with this camera. I like the riotous colors, though they do provide camouflage, they also mimic/mirror the colors of the subject. Another consideration is that this is only a 3MP original -- cropping would probably limit me to 5x7 prints, even with a border. I can try fading the BG to make the butterfly pop out a bit more, and maybe I''ll try a vertical crop as well -- thanks for the sugggestion.', '2006-02-01 15:24:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(2111149, 275355, 45790, '<td valign="top">It''s over-enhanced. Best to avoid "auto" anything in post-processing and do it all by hand to get the most natural look.<br/></td>', 'It''s over-enhanced. Best to avoid "auto" anything in post-processing and do it all by hand to get the most natural look.', '2006-02-01 15:25:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2111161, 276779, 45790, '<td valign="top">Imagine it cropped so that only the bees and the one flower are in the frame. The bench, tree trunks, and the second flower are just distractions.</td>', 'Imagine it cropped so that only the bees and the one flower are in the frame. The bench, tree trunks, and the second flower are just distractions.', '2006-02-01 15:28:24.000000', NULL, 0),
