(2116288, 278952, 1847, '<td valign="top">I was completely swamped during the voting for this challenge, and didn''t have time to make a single comment.  In fact, I''m letting my membership lapse for now, as I don''t have the time to contribute to the site the way I should.<br/> <br/>With that said, I like this photo a lot.  The movement through the scene is really gripping, and the colors are great.  It woulda been neat to get this a bit earlier (or later?) in the day, to get the sun just a bit lower.</td>', 'I was completely swamped during the voting for this challenge, and didn''t have time to make a single comment.  In fact, I''m letting my membership lapse for now, as I don''t have the time to contribute to the site the way I should. With that said, I like this photo a lot.  The movement through the scene is really gripping, and the colors are great.  It woulda been neat to get this a bit earlier (or later?) in the day, to get the sun just a bit lower.', '2006-02-02 22:33:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2116300, 274727, 1847, '<td valign="top">I was completely swamped during the voting for this challenge, and didn''t have time to make a single comment.  In fact, I''m letting my membership lapse for now, as I don''t have the time to contribute to the site the way I should.<br/> <br/>I like this one a lot.  (I''m working to be a professional photographer, of children amongst other things, so this appeals to me.)  Candid shots are the best, and this certainly qualifies.  The only suggestion I might make is to leave a bit more negative space in there.  That is, zoom out a bit on this one.  The background is pretty interesting, and while it might overpower the girl, I think it might be worth investigating.<br/> <br/>Love the oversaturated, overexposed look, too.</td>', 'I was completely swamped during the voting for this challenge, and didn''t have time to make a single comment.  In fact, I''m letting my membership lapse for now, as I don''t have the time to contribute to the site the way I should. I like this one a lot.  (I''m working to be a professional photographer, of children amongst other things, so this appeals to me.)  Candid shots are the best, and this certainly qualifies.  The only suggestion I might make is to leave a bit more negative space in there.  That is, zoom out a bit on this one.  The background is pretty interesting, and while it might overpower the girl, I think it might be worth investigating. Love the oversaturated, overexposed look, too.', '2006-02-02 22:35:37.000000', NULL, 0),
