(2116836, 280642, 40718, '<td valign="top">I liked this shot.  I thought the technicals were excellent.  Lighting is nice and bright, but not overexposed.  Sharpness is quite excellent.  I found the rear bird to be distracting in two ways.  A) I don''t really like the way he''s holding his head (but it''s not like you can coach him).  B) more importantly, I don''t really like that he''s not in the DOF.  He is just as well lit as the first and commands almost as much space in the frame.  I just wish he was a "subject" as well.  The soft focus makes his eyes all weird too.<br/> <br/>But really overall and excellent shot.</td>', 'I liked this shot.  I thought the technicals were excellent.  Lighting is nice and bright, but not overexposed.  Sharpness is quite excellent.  I found the rear bird to be distracting in two ways.  A) I don''t really like the way he''s holding his head (but it''s not like you can coach him).  B) more importantly, I don''t really like that he''s not in the DOF.  He is just as well lit as the first and commands almost as much space in the frame.  I just wish he was a "subject" as well.  The soft focus makes his eyes all weird too. But really overall and excellent shot.', '2006-02-03 00:50:34.000000', NULL, 0),
