(2124246, 275213, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>It''s always a delight to draw a beautifully done image from the Critique Club queue.  I get the chance to examine a lovely photograph.<br/> <br/>But I can hardly improve on the comments you have already received so I won''t try.  Except to add that your sky is perfectly fine.  There is no real need to polarize the daylights out of every sky in creation.  However, I would probably have used the clone tool on that aircraft condensation trail in the upper left corner.<br/> <br/>Your portfolio tells me you are a good photographer.  If you have the time, we sure could use your expertise in the Critique Club.  <br/> <br/>In any event,  I shall look forward to seeing more of your work in DPC.<br/> <br/>(oh, yes.  er, bathtub???)<br/>;&gt;)</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  It''s always a delight to draw a beautifully done image from the Critique Club queue.  I get the chance to examine a lovely photograph. But I can hardly improve on the comments you have already received so I won''t try.  Except to add that your sky is perfectly fine.  There is no real need to polarize the daylights out of every sky in creation.  However, I would probably have used the clone tool on that aircraft condensation trail in the upper left corner. Your portfolio tells me you are a good photographer.  If you have the time, we sure could use your expertise in the Critique Club.   In any event,  I shall look forward to seeing more of your work in DPC. (oh, yes.  er, bathtub???);>)', '2006-02-05 14:39:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(2124405, 275519, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi I am Kari from the critique club.  Hopefully this is painless for you.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>I wish we had skys like that here ... beautiful.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I like the composition, the log being on thirds works, the colours are wonderful.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Hard to be off subject on best of, and you weren''t met and excelled in fact.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour, focus, and light):</b> <br/>Nature provides well.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Top 60 finish ... and out of over 800 ... I would not know how to grow the vote ... I think that this is a fantastic finish.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Looks like you should keep happening across these shots as you seem to.  Keep hiking it seems to also inspire you.<br/> <br/>Any questions on the critique feel free to PM me.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/>Kari<br/></td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi I am Kari from the critique club.  Hopefully this is painless for you. First Impression - the most important one: I wish we had skys like that here ... beautiful. Composition: I like the composition, the log being on thirds works, the colours are wonderful. Subject: Hard to be off subject on best of, and you weren''t met and excelled in fact. Technical (Colour, focus, and light): Nature provides well. To grow its vote?: Top 60 finish ... and out of over 800 ... I would not know how to grow the vote ... I think that this is a fantastic finish. Summary: Looks like you should keep happening across these shots as you seem to.  Keep hiking it seems to also inspire you. Any questions on the critique feel free to PM me. CheersKari', '2006-02-05 16:20:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(2124421, 279446, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi<br/> <br/>Kari from the Critique Club, the following is a critique of your pic.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Lovely, and beatiful cityscape ... very peaceful picture.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I feel this is a little centred,  I also think that it needed to be.  the reflections are truely lovely and the impression from just looking at them is just fantastic as well.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Best of ... and you did well, not only on subject, but your overall second best scoring ... you are on the improve!<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour, focus, and light):</b> <br/>I love the out of the camera with just a little cropping shots.  To me this is what a lot of photography is about ... being able to show the reality as beautifully as you can ...<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>You did well ...  I don''t really know how to grow votes in the best of as it is such an open and personal thing to vote on.  With many fantastic shots in it.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>The impression is lovely, your portfolio is growing, keep it up you are producing some wonderful pics.<br/> <br/>If you have any comments of wish to further clarify the criqitue please feel free to PM  me.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi Kari from the Critique Club, the following is a critique of your pic. First Impression - the most important one: Lovely, and beatiful cityscape ... very peaceful picture. Composition: I feel this is a little centred,  I also think that it needed to be.  the reflections are truely lovely and the impression from just looking at them is just fantastic as well. Subject: Best of ... and you did well, not only on subject, but your overall second best scoring ... you are on the improve! Technical (Colour, focus, and light): I love the out of the camera with just a little cropping shots.  To me this is what a lot of photography is about ... being able to show the reality as beautifully as you can ... To grow its vote?: You did well ...  I don''t really know how to grow votes in the best of as it is such an open and personal thing to vote on.  With many fantastic shots in it. Summary: The impression is lovely, your portfolio is growing, keep it up you are producing some wonderful pics. If you have any comments of wish to further clarify the criqitue please feel free to PM  me. Cheers Kari', '2006-02-05 16:28:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2124430, 275667, 34659, '<td valign="top"><b>* Greetings from the Critique Club *</b> <br/>It figures I would get a fantastic shot like this to critique!  Finished 34th out of 829 with a final score of 6.756.  That''s REALLY something to be proud of in the field of Best of 2005 challenge entries.  Congratulations.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression:</b> <br/>Well, I scored this a 9 during the challenge.  My first impression was WOW and that it certainly had strong emotional appeal.<br/> <br/>That being said and upon closer inspection (and after reading the other comments given), I will do my best to provide some constructive feedback.  [Next time it might help the CC if you also left some photographer comments regarding your intentions, post-processing steps, etc. - Thanks!]<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I think this is probably the strongest point of the image.  You''ve got the foreground and background covered beautifully with plenty of things to keep the viewer engaged, yet never allowing him/her to take his/her eyes out of the frame.  The landscape in and of itself is exceptionally interesting and you captured it well.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>It''s tough to go wrong with a seascape, but tougher still to pull it off well - and you do.  There were several comments about the apparent lack of seagulls (vs the title) and I have to admit it crossed my mind during the challenge as well, but then I noticed them on top of the far rock.  Not sure if voters knocked anything off for this (I didn''t), but worth noting.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Color, focus, and light):</b> <br/>The unusual color tones really make this shot stand out, and while there were some differences of opinion regarding your choices here, I think it was a masterful stroke.  By going against the "normal" hues, you made this beautiful scene stand out even more.  The dark tones really added to the mood of the piece too, giving it much more emotional appeal.  Your lighting control is fantastic.  My only minor nit (and I mean tiny) was with the focus/DOF.  It seemed to me (and a couple of other commenters) that it was slightly off.  Of course, this didn''t seem to hurt your score too much.  :-)<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Not sure what else you could have done here outside of slightly sharper focus and including more visible birds.  Again, your score was exceptionally good in an unusually large, very competitive challenge.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>From reviewing your profile &amp; portfolio, I''m not telling you anything that you don''t already know...  You''re an accomplished photographer already and have a great eye for composition.  You obviously have the technical savvy to pull off a winning shot (and will soon have the ribbons to prove it I''m sure!) - I think it''s just a matter of getting everything to click at the the right time in the right place.  :-)<br/> <br/>Congratulations again - beautiful job.<br/> <br/>Just my 2 cents...<br/> <br/>Jimmy</td>', '* Greetings from the Critique Club * It figures I would get a fantastic shot like this to critique!  Finished 34th out of 829 with a final score of 6.756.  That''s REALLY something to be proud of in the field of Best of 2005 challenge entries.  Congratulations. First Impression: Well, I scored this a 9 during the challenge.  My first impression was WOW and that it certainly had strong emotional appeal. That being said and upon closer inspection (and after reading the other comments given), I will do my best to provide some constructive feedback.  [Next time it might help the CC if you also left some photographer comments regarding your intentions, post-processing steps, etc. - Thanks!] Composition: I think this is probably the strongest point of the image.  You''ve got the foreground and background covered beautifully with plenty of things to keep the viewer engaged, yet never allowing him/her to take his/her eyes out of the frame.  The landscape in and of itself is exceptionally interesting and you captured it well. Subject: It''s tough to go wrong with a seascape, but tougher still to pull it off well - and you do.  There were several comments about the apparent lack of seagulls (vs the title) and I have to admit it crossed my mind during the challenge as well, but then I noticed them on top of the far rock.  Not sure if voters knocked anything off for this (I didn''t), but worth noting. Technical (Color, focus, and light): The unusual color tones really make this shot stand out, and while there were some differences of opinion regarding your choices here, I think it was a masterful stroke.  By going against the "normal" hues, you made this beautiful scene stand out even more.  The dark tones really added to the mood of the piece too, giving it much more emotional appeal.  Your lighting control is fantastic.  My only minor nit (and I mean tiny) was with the focus/DOF.  It seemed to me (and a couple of other commenters) that it was slightly off.  Of course, this didn''t seem to hurt your score too much.  :-) To grow its vote?: Not sure what else you could have done here outside of slightly sharper focus and including more visible birds.  Again, your score was exceptionally good in an unusually large, very competitive challenge. Summary: From reviewing your profile & portfolio, I''m not telling you anything that you don''t already know...  You''re an accomplished photographer already and have a great eye for composition.  You obviously have the technical savvy to pull off a winning shot (and will soon have the ribbons to prove it I''m sure!) - I think it''s just a matter of getting everything to click at the the right time in the right place.  :-) Congratulations again - beautiful job. Just my 2 cents... Jimmy', '2006-02-05 16:41:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2124468, 277530, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>What a startlingly nice image of the orange section.  When I saw this in competition, I scored it high, as did many of our voters.<br/> <br/>However, now that I''m in critique mode, I''ve got to be a bit more objective about your image.  You do have some commentors who noted the photoshop effects around the edges of your orange could use some work.  This unevenness shows up loud and clear on my monitor as well.  While I note you didn''t prefer to mark these particular comments as helpful, they really are meant to assist you.  As is this one.  There is a light blue halo all around the orange. There are peculiar two-color blue changes at the right side above the mirrored segment.  The blue at the bottom shows a marked color change where either erasures or some other changes in color took place.  Just a little more practice with PS is likely all it''ll take to make your images constant winners.<br/> <br/>Overall, a fine image, well placed in the frame and excellent focus. <br/> <br/>I see I''ve had the pleasure of critiquing another of your images recently and for sure, I''ll look forward to seeing more of your work on DPC!</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  What a startlingly nice image of the orange section.  When I saw this in competition, I scored it high, as did many of our voters. However, now that I''m in critique mode, I''ve got to be a bit more objective about your image.  You do have some commentors who noted the photoshop effects around the edges of your orange could use some work.  This unevenness shows up loud and clear on my monitor as well.  While I note you didn''t prefer to mark these particular comments as helpful, they really are meant to assist you.  As is this one.  There is a light blue halo all around the orange. There are peculiar two-color blue changes at the right side above the mirrored segment.  The blue at the bottom shows a marked color change where either erasures or some other changes in color took place.  Just a little more practice with PS is likely all it''ll take to make your images constant winners. Overall, a fine image, well placed in the frame and excellent focus.  I see I''ve had the pleasure of critiquing another of your images recently and for sure, I''ll look forward to seeing more of your work on DPC!', '2006-02-05 17:20:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2124515, 274786, 42125, '<td valign="top">The people that gave you "1" are probably offended in some way. Don''t let it spoil it for you.<br/>No. 126 of over 800 is pretty good but this was the best picture in my opinion. Yesterday I realized that I didn''t see in the top score and started to search for it. Disappointed in seeing it not among the best 20.<br/>Great colours, great shot, great caption, great humor, innocence. Everything that you want to see in a good picture.</td>', 'The people that gave you "1" are probably offended in some way. Don''t let it spoil it for you.No. 126 of over 800 is pretty good but this was the best picture in my opinion. Yesterday I realized that I didn''t see in the top score and started to search for it. Disappointed in seeing it not among the best 20.Great colours, great shot, great caption, great humor, innocence. Everything that you want to see in a good picture.', '2006-02-05 17:47:33.000000', NULL, 0),
