(2127755, 281524, 29156, '<td valign="top">great gray tones, sharpness and composition<br/>- I think the people do a lot for the picture, they add more feeling to it and a sense for the greatness of the nature - so I think you did right to not clone them away<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-02-06 20:00:18.</i></td>', 'great gray tones, sharpness and composition- I think the people do a lot for the picture, they add more feeling to it and a sense for the greatness of the nature - so I think you did right to not clone them away', '2006-02-06 19:57:19.000000', '2006-02-06 20:00:18.000000', 0),
(2127810, 281418, 42567, '<td valign="top">***Greetings from the Critique Club***<br/> <br/>First let me say this is a great picture!  I think if this picture would have been in a regular challenge and not a challenge with 800+ you probably would have finished in the top 25 if not better.  Many people get tired after voting a while and start giving 4''s and 5''s.  <br/> <br/>Anyway, back to the picture.  The best thing about the shot is the awesome sunset.  The clouds give such a great feel to the picture. The sunset reflecting off the lake adds another pop to the picture.  I also like how your mountain tops are different sizes.  It really moves my eyes up and down, which I think is good.<br/> <br/>The only thing I can find wrong with the picture is the lighting.  Maybe a little bit more light may have helped.  I think you lose detail when the picture is a little bit dark.  Just my opinion.<br/> <br/>I hope this critique helps!<br/>Phillip</td>', '***Greetings from the Critique Club*** First let me say this is a great picture!  I think if this picture would have been in a regular challenge and not a challenge with 800+ you probably would have finished in the top 25 if not better.  Many people get tired after voting a while and start giving 4''s and 5''s.   Anyway, back to the picture.  The best thing about the shot is the awesome sunset.  The clouds give such a great feel to the picture. The sunset reflecting off the lake adds another pop to the picture.  I also like how your mountain tops are different sizes.  It really moves my eyes up and down, which I think is good. The only thing I can find wrong with the picture is the lighting.  Maybe a little bit more light may have helped.  I think you lose detail when the picture is a little bit dark.  Just my opinion. I hope this critique helps!Phillip', '2006-02-06 20:27:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2127945, 282008, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Boating and Biking is another interesting piece in the Best of 2005.  I think this was an extremely tough challenge since there were 829 submission, and because of this a lot of piece did not get the attention they should.<br/> <br/>I really like the overall composition of your shot,it is a subdued but warm shot.   The subject and shot have a great sense of summer and all the pleasure and simplifies of being young.  The yellow flowers give the shot extra attention, if they were not included I think viewers might over look it. I think I would try differnt cropping to see if it enhances the shot or takes too much of the subject away.  I think the shapes give a great feel and even flow to the shot.  Good work.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-02-06 21:26:21.</i></td>', '*Critique Club* Boating and Biking is another interesting piece in the Best of 2005.  I think this was an extremely tough challenge since there were 829 submission, and because of this a lot of piece did not get the attention they should. I really like the overall composition of your shot,it is a subdued but warm shot.   The subject and shot have a great sense of summer and all the pleasure and simplifies of being young.  The yellow flowers give the shot extra attention, if they were not included I think viewers might over look it. I think I would try differnt cropping to see if it enhances the shot or takes too much of the subject away.  I think the shapes give a great feel and even flow to the shot.  Good work.', '2006-02-06 21:23:10.000000', '2006-02-06 21:26:21.000000', 0),
(2127976, 274847, 12311, '<td valign="top">I haven''t taken the time to read through all the comments here (...I can''t take my eyes off your photo long enough to do so).  If it hasn''t already been said (and I can''t imagine it hasn''t), this image belongs on the cover of National Geographic.  Absolutely awe-inspiring!!!  Congratulations, Lynn.<br/> <br/>-len</td>', 'I haven''t taken the time to read through all the comments here (...I can''t take my eyes off your photo long enough to do so).  If it hasn''t already been said (and I can''t imagine it hasn''t), this image belongs on the cover of National Geographic.  Absolutely awe-inspiring!!!  Congratulations, Lynn. -len', '2006-02-06 21:39:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2127987, 279012, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Lake Yellowstone is a nice landscape piece.  I think it was a great capture and placement of the trees, the nice off centered balance is prefect for me.  It is very interesting how white the trees appear, it really makes the shot seem cold.  I think this was an extremely hard category, especially with 800+ entries.  I might have turned up the contrast and played with burning and or dodging to see what the image could be with some editing.  I think catching the dark sky with the clouds really lets this become a better landscape shot and possibly enhancing this in contrast to striking trees.  I am surprised you picked such a light piece looking at your other shots but good work on this one.</td>', '*Critique Club* Lake Yellowstone is a nice landscape piece.  I think it was a great capture and placement of the trees, the nice off centered balance is prefect for me.  It is very interesting how white the trees appear, it really makes the shot seem cold.  I think this was an extremely hard category, especially with 800+ entries.  I might have turned up the contrast and played with burning and or dodging to see what the image could be with some editing.  I think catching the dark sky with the clouds really lets this become a better landscape shot and possibly enhancing this in contrast to striking trees.  I am surprised you picked such a light piece looking at your other shots but good work on this one.', '2006-02-06 21:42:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(2128301, 280263, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>" Hangin'' Out" is a great shot.  I really love this perspective.  The subject is amazing and the girl just demands attention.  The soft glow and focus is excellent for these children.<br/> <br/>I would have really liked to see this shot with a little more contrast, and I really think it would have bumped the score up.  Color especially with children always seems to give it just a little more.<br/> <br/>This was a great piece because it was different and not the run of the mill entry.  The overall composition of this shot is excellent, I don''t think you could have possibly cropped it any better.  Good work.</td>', '*Critique Club* " Hangin'' Out" is a great shot.  I really love this perspective.  The subject is amazing and the girl just demands attention.  The soft glow and focus is excellent for these children. I would have really liked to see this shot with a little more contrast, and I really think it would have bumped the score up.  Color especially with children always seems to give it just a little more. This was a great piece because it was different and not the run of the mill entry.  The overall composition of this shot is excellent, I don''t think you could have possibly cropped it any better.  Good work.', '2006-02-06 22:51:13.000000', NULL, 0),
