(2128997, 275849, 37430, '<td valign="top"><i>Greetings from the Critique Club!</i> <br/> <br/><b>Aesthetic:</b>Beautiful capture. The smooth edges and crisp focus makes this image great. It has almost zen like style - minimalistic. The touch of blue actually adds the punch.<br/> <br/><b>Technical:</b>Well exposed, good contrast, crisp focus. Period.<br/> <br/><b>Challenge:</b>Anything would fit into this challenge theme, so no comments :)<br/> <br/><b>Conclusion:</b>Overall a good compostion. I liked the simplicity of the photo but I feel its a bit "busy" due to lots of things to focus on. Maybe a tighter crop could help. Somehow I feel this should have scored more. I did not voted for this challenge but would have given something between 6-7 on this one.<br/> <br/>I''m by no means expert in area of photography. My comments are purely based on my limited understanding of technology and art behind digital photography. Apart from doing detailed evaluation of your submission, my intent is to learn different styles of photography by critically evaluating selective submissions. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via email or PM.<br/> <br/>Wish you a great day!<br/><b><i>-Tej</i></b></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  Aesthetic:Beautiful capture. The smooth edges and crisp focus makes this image great. It has almost zen like style - minimalistic. The touch of blue actually adds the punch. Technical:Well exposed, good contrast, crisp focus. Period. Challenge:Anything would fit into this challenge theme, so no comments :) Conclusion:Overall a good compostion. I liked the simplicity of the photo but I feel its a bit "busy" due to lots of things to focus on. Maybe a tighter crop could help. Somehow I feel this should have scored more. I did not voted for this challenge but would have given something between 6-7 on this one. I''m by no means expert in area of photography. My comments are purely based on my limited understanding of technology and art behind digital photography. Apart from doing detailed evaluation of your submission, my intent is to learn different styles of photography by critically evaluating selective submissions. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via email or PM. Wish you a great day!-Tej', '2006-02-07 07:29:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2129009, 279371, 37430, '<td valign="top"><i>Greetings from the Critique Club!</i> <br/> <br/><b>Aesthetic:</b>Nice photo. Almost has an abstract feel to it. Slightly lacks on composition.<br/> <br/><b>Technical:</b>Too shallow a DOF. Even the head is not fully in focus. Not that shallow DOF was not required for this one, but there is no single part of body which is fully in focus which does not let me focus my eyes on one point.<br/> <br/><b>Challenge:</b>Offcourse anything would fit into this challenge theme ...so no comments :)<br/> <br/><b>Conclusion:</b> I feel that only if the head was in focus and you would have followed rule-of-thirds, this might have scored much higher. And yes- this one lacks on uniqueness as there are lots of similar shots available on net and over DPC.<br/> <br/>I wonder how were you able to get such shallow DOF with f5.0 ...<br/> <br/>I''m by no means expert in area of photography. My comments are purely based on my limited understanding of technology and art behind digital photography. Apart from doing detailed evaluation of your submission, my intent is to learn different styles of photography by critically evaluating selective submissions. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via email or PM.<br/> <br/>Wish you a great day!<br/><b><i>-Tej</i></b></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  Aesthetic:Nice photo. Almost has an abstract feel to it. Slightly lacks on composition. Technical:Too shallow a DOF. Even the head is not fully in focus. Not that shallow DOF was not required for this one, but there is no single part of body which is fully in focus which does not let me focus my eyes on one point. Challenge:Offcourse anything would fit into this challenge theme ...so no comments :) Conclusion: I feel that only if the head was in focus and you would have followed rule-of-thirds, this might have scored much higher. And yes- this one lacks on uniqueness as there are lots of similar shots available on net and over DPC. I wonder how were you able to get such shallow DOF with f5.0 ... I''m by no means expert in area of photography. My comments are purely based on my limited understanding of technology and art behind digital photography. Apart from doing detailed evaluation of your submission, my intent is to learn different styles of photography by critically evaluating selective submissions. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via email or PM. Wish you a great day!-Tej', '2006-02-07 07:37:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2129034, 276302, 37430, '<td valign="top"><i>Greetings from the Critique Club!</i> <br/> <br/><b>Aesthetic:</b>Overall I fee this is an average compostion. Not because there are too many kitty pictures on DPC, but somehow this one is too "flat"<br/> <br/><b>Technical:</b>Again - too flat a picture. It needed more contrast. Also DOF is shallow. There are parts which are not in focus.<br/> <br/><b>Challenge:</b>Well..anything would fit in for this challenge theme ..so no comments :)<br/> <br/><b>Conclusion:</b>I feel working with "levels" in photoshop would add some contrast and will imrove the "depth" of otherwise "flat" composition. Details on background can be little distracting sometimes.<br/> <br/>But offcourse- the kitty is cute :)<br/> <br/>I''m by no means expert in area of photography. My comments are purely based on my limited understanding of technology and art behind digital photography. Apart from doing detailed evaluation of your submission, my intent is to learn different styles  of photography by critically evaluating selective submissions. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via email or PM.<br/> <br/>Wish you a great day!<br/><b><i>-Tej</i></b></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  Aesthetic:Overall I fee this is an average compostion. Not because there are too many kitty pictures on DPC, but somehow this one is too "flat" Technical:Again - too flat a picture. It needed more contrast. Also DOF is shallow. There are parts which are not in focus. Challenge:Well..anything would fit in for this challenge theme ..so no comments :) Conclusion:I feel working with "levels" in photoshop would add some contrast and will imrove the "depth" of otherwise "flat" composition. Details on background can be little distracting sometimes. But offcourse- the kitty is cute :) I''m by no means expert in area of photography. My comments are purely based on my limited understanding of technology and art behind digital photography. Apart from doing detailed evaluation of your submission, my intent is to learn different styles  of photography by critically evaluating selective submissions. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via email or PM. Wish you a great day!-Tej', '2006-02-07 07:44:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2129053, 276584, 37430, '<td valign="top"><i>Greetings from the Critique Club!</i> <br/> <br/><b>Aesthetic:</b> Beautiful capture. You were at right place at right moment for this one. Very pleasing photo with just one subject to focus on. The background of smoke and dark sky compliments the contrasting color of biplane.<br/> <br/><b>Technical:</b> Not much comments but I feel white balance needs to be adjusted. It seems to be little towards colder side.<br/> <br/><b>Challenge:</b> Well...anything would fit into this challenge theme..so no comments on this one :)<br/> <br/><b>Conclusion:</b> I feel a bit of warmer color balance, some dodging on plane (maybe some saturation and sharpening too..only for plane) and following rule of thirds will make it ideal poster picture. This is strong composition which needs complimentary post-processing.<br/> <br/>I''m by no means expert in area of photography. My comments are purely based on my limited understanding of technology and art behind digital photography. Apart from doing detailed evaluation of your submission, my intent is to learn different styles  of photography by critically evaluating selective submissions. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via email or PM.<br/> <br/>Wish you a great day!<br/><b><i>-Tej</i></b></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  Aesthetic: Beautiful capture. You were at right place at right moment for this one. Very pleasing photo with just one subject to focus on. The background of smoke and dark sky compliments the contrasting color of biplane. Technical: Not much comments but I feel white balance needs to be adjusted. It seems to be little towards colder side. Challenge: Well...anything would fit into this challenge theme..so no comments on this one :) Conclusion: I feel a bit of warmer color balance, some dodging on plane (maybe some saturation and sharpening too..only for plane) and following rule of thirds will make it ideal poster picture. This is strong composition which needs complimentary post-processing. I''m by no means expert in area of photography. My comments are purely based on my limited understanding of technology and art behind digital photography. Apart from doing detailed evaluation of your submission, my intent is to learn different styles  of photography by critically evaluating selective submissions. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via email or PM. Wish you a great day!-Tej', '2006-02-07 07:59:09.000000', NULL, 0),
