(2195443, 277252, 45343, '<td valign="top">Composition: There is great placement of the subject in the rule of thirds placement.  The leading lines created by the cross also guide the eye back to the subject.   Personally, I might have given either a tighter crop on the right or wider on the left to give some symmetry to the cross.<br/> <br/>Subject:  This is probably what made you score less then you expected   In a similar thread, I asked for feedback, and the only comments were that a static statue as a subject matter was scored down.  <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=353003&amp;highlight=free%20study" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">See Here</a> <br/>Personally, I like your subject, but it does take a moment to visually extract the subject from the cross due to the blending color.<br/> <br/>Hope this helps.<br/></td>', 'Composition: There is great placement of the subject in the rule of thirds placement.  The leading lines created by the cross also guide the eye back to the subject.   Personally, I might have given either a tighter crop on the right or wider on the left to give some symmetry to the cross. Subject:  This is probably what made you score less then you expected   In a similar thread, I asked for feedback, and the only comments were that a static statue as a subject matter was scored down.  See Here Personally, I like your subject, but it does take a moment to visually extract the subject from the cross due to the blending color. Hope this helps.', '2006-03-02 07:36:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2196343, 277252, 49672, '<td valign="top">Rating (and critiquing) pictures of statues is tough, because I like to see something added in the photograph that extends the original intent of the sculptor.  I think the angle addresses this, but only slightly.  Perhaps this would have performed better with a dramatic thunderstorm in the background, or a rainbow, or a sunburst coming through a cloud, to add new meaning and context to the image.<br/>As it is, the technical aspects of the shot are fine, and it isn''t an unpleasant image.  I would have pegged it at a 5 or 6.</td>', 'Rating (and critiquing) pictures of statues is tough, because I like to see something added in the photograph that extends the original intent of the sculptor.  I think the angle addresses this, but only slightly.  Perhaps this would have performed better with a dramatic thunderstorm in the background, or a rainbow, or a sunburst coming through a cloud, to add new meaning and context to the image.As it is, the technical aspects of the shot are fine, and it isn''t an unpleasant image.  I would have pegged it at a 5 or 6.', '2006-03-02 16:01:37.000000', NULL, 0),
