(2696669, 281099, 12253, '<td valign="top">Great shot Ray!  I so wanted to go there when we were in Maine last summer, but didn''t make it there.  It was hard enough convincing my family to go with me to Bass Harbor lighthouse.<br/> <br/>I see you got some complaints about oversharpening/haloing on the rocks.  Have you tried Focus Magic (there''s a free trial, lets you do 5 photos).  I like the way it sharpens better than USM.  Doesn''t seem to halo, at least at lower sharpening settings which is more than enough.  Works very well just after you reduce to 640.  (And you can also apply it before reducing, if you want uber-sharp.)</td>', 'Great shot Ray!  I so wanted to go there when we were in Maine last summer, but didn''t make it there.  It was hard enough convincing my family to go with me to Bass Harbor lighthouse. I see you got some complaints about oversharpening/haloing on the rocks.  Have you tried Focus Magic (there''s a free trial, lets you do 5 photos).  I like the way it sharpens better than USM.  Doesn''t seem to halo, at least at lower sharpening settings which is more than enough.  Works very well just after you reduce to 640.  (And you can also apply it before reducing, if you want uber-sharp.)', '2006-08-05 01:19:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2713426, 279330, 43432, '<td valign="top">amazing!!!!</td>', 'amazing!!!!', '2006-08-10 02:05:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2716327, 280443, 41999, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=290002" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/41999/thumb/290002.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/41999/thumb/290002.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/41999/thumb/290002.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>This is an alternate rendition of the challenge photograph. I have tried to improve the image by taking into consideration comments during voting.<br/> <br/>The day was overcast which expressed itself in the color of the water...a warm, dark grey. Several commenters during voting commented that the water was too saturated or desaturated. Since it couldn''t be both, I took this to mean that the picture should have more color or a wider range of colors. Others thought the image too dark.<br/> <br/>In the version that appeared in the challenge, my intent was to emphasize the relatively quite small subject, which I did largely by increasing contrast using levels and curves in Photoshop.</td>', '  This is an alternate rendition of the challenge photograph. I have tried to improve the image by taking into consideration comments during voting. The day was overcast which expressed itself in the color of the water...a warm, dark grey. Several commenters during voting commented that the water was too saturated or desaturated. Since it couldn''t be both, I took this to mean that the picture should have more color or a wider range of colors. Others thought the image too dark. In the version that appeared in the challenge, my intent was to emphasize the relatively quite small subject, which I did largely by increasing contrast using levels and curves in Photoshop.', '2006-08-11 00:06:10.000000', NULL, 0),
